# Chargrp.dat of Gracia Final: the layout of High Five with four rows of hair in place of five. Read on two Gracia
# Final clients. The Engine.dll of one of them keeps the number of rows too,
# FL2CharData::HairAcceStyleNum: 4, where High Five 273 has 5.
format  1
file    Chargrp.dat
title   Gracia Final
like    High Five

replace rows {
    list 4 rows {                   # rows of hair. The first is the hair a player chooses, and a hair accessory
                                    # picks another by its mesh name, see HairRows
        list 15 styles {            # one for each hair style, from 0. A style the figure does not have is empty
            Hair    front           # the hair over the forehead, such as Fighter.MFighter_m000_m00_ah
            Hair    back            # the hair at the back of the head, such as Fighter.MFighter_m000_m00_bh
        }
    }
}
